repository only; the model files it loads are under their own licenses, below.

The page loads, at run time, ONNX files derived from works by others, hosted at
https://huggingface.co/ozcancelik/antalia-1-onnx:

- Antalia 1 by Sezgin Saygili, Emre Kaplaner, Oncel Ozgul and Fikri San Koktas (Patientdesk.ai),
  Antalia OpenRAIL-M. https://huggingface.co/cloud0day3/antalia-1, https://github.com/0daycloud/antalia
  Modifications: converted to ONNX (text, flow, vocoder graphs), the released voice baked in,
  partly converted to fp16. The full list is in the model card of the repository above.
  Use of the model and its output is subject to the use-based restrictions of that license.

- BigVGAN v2 (nvidia/bigvgan_v2_24khz_100band_256x) by NVIDIA, MIT.
  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/bigvgan_v2_24khz_100band_256x

normalize.js is a JavaScript port of turkish_tts/normalize.py, and tts.js reimplements the
chunking and sampling of turkish_tts/crossflow*.py, from https://github.com/0daycloud/antalia
(Apache-2.0).

aura.js comes from ema-lightning-web by the same author.

onnxruntime-web (MIT, Microsoft) is loaded from a CDN at run time and is not redistributed here.
